course: dictionary
lesson: 16090
title: Wasted and waste
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Wasted» comes from the word waste. It means used badly, used carelessly, or lost without being useful. «I left the tap running, so a lot of water was wasted.» The water went down the drain and did nothing useful.
explain: You can also use «wasted» for time or chances. «We waited an hour for a bus that never came. What a wasted hour!» Nothing good came from that hour. «Waste» can be a noun too, meaning rubbish or things thrown away, as in «Please put the waste in the bin.»
explain: To check the meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. «The lights were on all day in the empty room, so the electricity was wasted.» If you think wasted means used for nothing useful, the sentence still makes sense, so you have got it.
fact: Wasted means used badly or carelessly, or lost without being useful.
fact: A wasted trip or a wasted chance brought nothing good.
fact: «Go to waste» means not used and thrown away, as in «Don't let the food go to waste.»
fact: In maths, you can take away the wasted amount to find what is left: total minus wasted.
fact: Saving energy, recycling and turning off lights all mean less is wasted.
exercise: «We wasted our lunch money on sweets we did not even like.» What does wasted mean? | Counted twice | Given away to a friend | Saved carefully in a box | *Used badly, spent for nothing useful
exercise: «The trip was a wasted journey, and the shop was closed.» Find and copy the word that means lost without being useful. | trip | closed | *wasted | journey
exercise: A tank had 20 litres of water. 6 litres were wasted through a leak. How many litres are left? | 6 litres | 26 litres | 20 litres | *14 litres
test: «Turning off the lights saves energy, so less electricity is wasted.» What does wasted mean here? | Turned on again | Shared with friends | *Used up for nothing useful | Counted carefully
test: Which phrase means a trip that brought nothing good? | *A wasted trip | A happy trip | A cheap trip | A long trip
exam: Which is a good way to stop food being wasted? | Buy more food than you need every day | Leave the fridge door open | Throw away leftovers without thinking | *Eat or freeze leftovers before they go off
